The only newsgroup that does not appear to be available at UBC is 
alt.fan.karla-homulka, but most others that were the subject of 
contraversy in 1992 appear to be available now.  Last year when the 
newsgroup alt.fan.karla-homulka was banned, I managed to get the 
necessary information through anonymous ftp, but while playing around 
with www starting at UBC, I somehow found my way onto a Danish www server 
on which it was possible to read material from newsgroup 
alt.fan.karla-homulka.  Thus, even when the university has an explicit 
policy of barring access to information the same facilities of the 
university allow anyone using lynx to access this data in a roundabout 
way.  As various internet services grow I'm sure that it will become even 
easier to access such forbidden data as no-one really knows all of the 
paths which are available from one information source to another.

